       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_gha_162'), 2, 'Look at what `id-token: write` enables, at the `role-to-assume` input of the AWS credentials action, at the difference between `@v4` and `@<40-hex SHA>`, and at the `env:` key of a step.'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_gha_162'), 3, 'A step that greets the author of an issue without injection: `env: { TITLE: "${{ github.event.issue.title }}" }` and `run: echo "New issue: $TITLE"`. A job that uploads to Google Cloud through OIDC: `permissions: { contents: read, id-token: write }` and `google-github-actions/auth@<sha> # v2` with `workload_identity_provider` instead of a JSON key.');
